s of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 12 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4 & 12 & 5\\end{aligned}]=6\\cdot 2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 5=-180.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-180|=180.\n$$" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347228 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347229 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347230 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347231 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347232 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1041 "selection" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347228 13194139535400 true] [17592186347227 1110 #uuid "97e15ba0-f9f3-507b-a74f-8b4e8c28599b" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347228 1034 "180" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347228 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347228 1111 #uuid "c76f69a0-62bd-5cea-b895-3f3730f15f4b" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347229 1034 "240" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347229 1111 #uuid "348b0227-334e-5577-93dd-af0ef8272c08" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347230 1034 "120" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347230 1111 #uuid "074b5f9c-8c8d-5bcd-b5cf-4b402d85e997" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347231 1034 "160" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347231 1111 #uuid "b6513299-920a-5292-834a-4e68943878dc" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347232 1034 "200" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347232 1111 #uuid "82c32a38-4726-509a-b787-67d3864ffb3d" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347233 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347234 13194139535400 true] [17592186347233 1089 "q-69981" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347233 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535400 true] [17592186347233 1100 "Find the determinant of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347233 1113 #uuid "e78624d1-2a00-5991-bf80-759a76809215" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347233 1145 "Notice that the $2$nd column contains three zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd column of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (2\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(8-(-12)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347235 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347236 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347237 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347238 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347239 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1041 "selection" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347239 13194139535400 true] [17592186347234 1110 #uuid "b23bec3f-f491-520c-be30-b0a0056da076" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347235 1034 "-40" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347235 1111 #uuid "85268355-18b0-565a-a2c9-4f4632b46572" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347236 1034 "60" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347236 1111 #uuid "f065d1a6-343c-550a-842a-84e28779d356" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347237 1034 "-16" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347237 1111 #uuid "23ba8b71-67ba-59de-9558-e563c236a3f8" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347238 1034 "16" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347238 1111 #uuid "d9900669-95a1-520c-98bd-9b83b3891140" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347239 1034 "80" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535400 true] [17592186347239 1111 #uuid "d08b670d-0214-5f85-af01-62a9914df2ab" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347240 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347241 13194139535400 true] [17592186347240 1089 "q-70105" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347240 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535400 true] [17592186347240 1100 "Given that $det({A}^{T})=8$, which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=0$\n- $2\\text{det}(A)+\\text{det}(I)=16$\n- $3\\text{det}(I)-2\\text{det}(A)=-13$" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347240 1113 #uuid "5d58754e-8226-5acc-a0e9-1892373e3daa" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347240 1145 "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)=\\text{det}({A}^{T})=8\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=8-8=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. We have\n\n$$\n2\\text{det}(A)+\\text{det}(I)=2\\cdot 8+1=17\\ne 16.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n3\\text{det}(I)-2\\text{det}(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 8=-13.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347242 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347243 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347244 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347245 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347246 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1041 "selection" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347243 13194139535400 true] [17592186347241 1110 #uuid "1e133114-78d2-502e-96ce-9d176056d12c" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347242 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535400 true] [17592186347242 1111 #uuid "d69f49cf-30fa-558d-ac2e-04d0bc584b08" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347243 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535400 true] [17592186347243 1111 #uuid "fd3b1683-d36f-5b3e-b929-d2ca43a1c001" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347244 1034 "I only" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535400 true] [17592186347244 1111 #uuid "49ce8d43-3db1-518f-bc5a-06c6d8464625" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347245 1034 "III only" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535400 true] [17592186347245 1111 #uuid "f1e43d10-d7ff-5819-acf2-8a076187c080" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347246 1034 "II only" 13194139535400 true] [17592186347246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535400 true] [1